{
 "arc": [
  {
   "slide": 1,
   "title": "BeanBox: The Roastery Behind the Subscription",
   "point": "BeanBox is a high-velocity specialty coffee subscription in Kyiv, combining artisanal roasting with data-driven growth to capture the home-brewing boom.",
   "evidence": [
    "f1",
    "f5",
    "f8"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 2,
   "title": "Traction: 400 Subscribers in 6 Months",
   "point": "We have validated product-market fit with rapid early adoption, generating 7,200 EUR in monthly recurring revenue (MRR) with 400 paying subscribers.",
   "evidence": [
    "f2",
    "f3",
    "f4",
    "f5"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 3,
   "title": "The Team: Quality Meets Growth",
   "point": "Our founders cover the two critical pillars of a successful DTC brand: a master roaster ensuring product excellence and a growth marketer driving efficient acquisition.",
   "evidence": [
    "f8",
    "f23"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 4,
   "title": "Market Opportunity: Kyiv’s Specialty Shift",
   "point": "Kyiv’s coffee culture has shifted towards premium home brewing, creating a dense competitive landscape that validates demand for curated subscription models.",
   "evidence": [
    "f11",
    "f13",
    "f19"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 5,
   "title": "The Bottleneck: Capacity Constraint",
   "point": "Our current roastery is operating at capacity; we cannot fulfill existing demand or scale further without additional production infrastructure.",
   "evidence": [
    "f22"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 6,
   "title": "The Solution: A Second Roastery",
   "point": "Opening a second roastery is the specific, necessary step to unlock scale, remove production bottlenecks, and support a larger subscriber base.",
   "evidence": [
    "f7",
    "f22"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 7,
   "title": "Competitive Landscape",
   "point": "We operate in a mature market with established players like Kyiv City Roastery and Kolo Coffee, proving the viability of the subscription model in Kyiv.",
   "evidence": [
    "f11",
    "f15",
    "f20"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 8,
   "title": "Business Model: Recurring Revenue",
   "point": "Our unit economics are built on a simple, recurring 18 EUR/month subscription, creating predictable revenue streams from day one.",
   "evidence": [
    "f3",
    "f4"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 9,
   "title": "The Ask: 300k EUR",
   "point": "We are raising 300,000 EUR to fund the construction and equipment of our second roastery, enabling us to scale beyond our current 400-subscriber limit.",
   "evidence": [
    "f6",
    "f7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "slide": 10,
   "title": "Why Now?",
   "point": "With proven traction, a strong team, and a clear capacity bottleneck, this is the optimal moment to invest in infrastructure that directly enables growth.",
   "evidence": [
    "f5",
    "f22",
    "f23"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "why": "This order persuades by leading with the strongest proof of concept: rapid traction (400 subs in 6 months). By establishing the team's complementary skills early, it builds confidence in execution. The narrative then pivots to the 'why now'—the capacity constraint—making the need for a second roastery a logical necessity rather than just an expansion plan. This frames the 300k EUR ask not as a risk, but as a solution to a verified bottleneck."
}
